d=newdoc('XRP hybrid feature attribution verification');d.add_paragraph('Consolidated review of saved E1B models completed 8 November 2026 Sydney time.')
d.add_paragraph(f'The refined analysis gives an average {S["mean_technical_share_equal_pass_weight"]:.2f}% technical and {S["mean_news_share_equal_pass_weight"]:.2f}% news attribution across five training seeds and two reference sets. The historical 66.2% technical and 33.8% sentiment split is not confirmed for this corrected model and explanation design. These are shares of absolute model attribution, not percentages of price movement, explained variance or forecasting improvement.')
d.add_heading('Scope and numerical outcome',1)
table(d,['Item','Verified result'],[['Saved models','Five E1B checkpoints; no retraining'],['Explanations','1,000 fixed forecast origins per pass; ten passes'],['Inputs','30 hourly steps and 25 features; exact 24 hour return target'],['Training references','Two frozen sets of 32 training origins each'],['Completeness tolerance','9,948 of 10,000 pass; 52 retained failures'],['News share range',f'{S["news_share_range"][0]:.2f}% to {S["news_share_range"][1]:.2f}%'],['Seed SD of background averaged news shares',f'{S["news_seed_mean_sd"]:.2f} percentage points']])
d.add_paragraph('The 52 unresolved cases all occur for seed 42 and reference set 1. No case, seed or reference was removed from the primary result. Removing only failed cases as a sensitivity changes any pass share by at most 0.18 percentage points. Reference and seed sensitivity remain material even after the large improvement in numerical precision.')
d.add_heading('What is being explained',1)
d.add_paragraph('E1B is the preserved 570,497 parameter two layer BiLSTM, with 128 hidden units per direction, a 64 unit dense layer, dropout 0.2 and no attention. Nineteen technical and market inputs include the nine original indicators, real BTC close, OHLCV and existing derived technical variables. Six news inputs are direct sentiment, XRP specificity, XRP stance, uncertainty, hourly news presence and hours since the latest news capped at 48. Presence and recency are derived availability features; they are not GPT judgments.')
d.add_paragraph('The explained scalar is the unscaled predicted 24 hour log return. If z is the network output, the inverse target transform is rhat = (z - target_scaler.min_[0]) / target_scaler.scale_[0]. Price forecasts use Phat[t+24] = P[t] exp(rhat). This report attributes rhat; the price reconstruction and its direct current price factor are outside the explained function.')
d.add_heading('Interpretation for the research',1)
d.add_paragraph('The network uses both technical and news information, with technical inputs contributing more absolute attribution under this design. This does not establish that news improves forecasting. The separate matched final evaluation found E1B mean RMSE 0.042118 against E0 0.039976, a 5.36% deterioration. The evaluated period had prior historical exposure and is not a pristine prospective test. These attribution results must not be used to reverse that forecasting conclusion.')
pageheading(d,'Method and global importance')
d.add_paragraph('Expected integrated gradients averages an attribution path from each training reference b to the explained input x. For feature j and lag l, the attribution is the average over 32 references of (x[l,j] - b[l,j]) times the integral from zero to one of the derivative of the unscaled output along b + alpha (x - b). Gauss Legendre quadrature approximates the integral. This is a reference dependent expected gradient explanation, not exact combinatorial Shapley values. Paths between historical sequences can be unrealistic when features are correlated.')
d.add_paragraph('Each origin starts at 64 quadrature points. If the absolute completeness residual exceeds 0.00001 + 0.01 times the absolute output difference from the reference mean, the calculation uses 128 and then at most 256 points. All completed arrays are preserved. Global feature importance is mean over origins of the sum over all 30 lags of the absolute averaged attribution. The six news importances are summed and divided by total importance. Each pass receives equal weight in the headline mean; the alternative ratio after pooling absolute importances is 22.82% news. Absolute values are taken after reference averaging, so this is not the expectation of absolute reference specific contributions.')
picture(d,'GLOBAL_AND_STABILITY.png','Orange features are news inputs and blue features are technical inputs. Dashed line marks the historical 33.8% claim for comparison only.',6.4)
d.add_paragraph('Global rankings and contributions describe the saved models on this fixed random sample. They do not identify the economically best features or prove that removing a low attribution feature would improve forecasting. Correlated inputs can divide or exchange attribution credit. The pairwise Spearman correlation of full feature rankings ranges from 0.55 to 0.95 across the ten passes; seed and reference choice affect the ordering.')
pageheading(d,'Seed and reference stability')
table(d,['Seed','Reference','Technical percent','News percent','Failed cases'],[[int(r.seed),int(r.background),f'{r.technical_percent:.2f}',f'{r.news_percent:.2f}',int(r.failed_tolerance)] for _,r in C.iterrows()])
d.add_paragraph('Each seed is a training randomisation within the same historical market period. The five seeds are not independent market replications. The two background sets test a limited reference sensitivity; they do not span all possible background distributions. The reported range is descriptive and is not a confidence interval. The refined average differs from the first Monte Carlo estimate of approximately 21.75% news. Earlier arrays and reports remain archived rather than overwritten.')
picture(d,'CONVERGENCE.png','Left shows residual convergence on the original fixed 20 origin pilot for seed 42 and reference 0. Right compares original Monte Carlo shares with the refined estimates for every pass.',6.4)
d.add_paragraph('On the pilot, mean absolute residual decreases from 0.000522 at 16 quadrature points to 0.000219 at 32 and 0.000056 at 64. The full analysis uses adaptive refinement up to 256. Completeness is necessary but not sufficient for featurewise convergence: errors in different features can cancel. The pilot and residual checks improve confidence in the calculation without establishing exact SHAP values or universal stability.')
pageheading(d,'Temporal and news conditioned attribution')
picture(d,'TEMPORAL.png','Lag zero is the forecast origin and lag minus 29 is the oldest input hour. The heatmap feature order is saved with each raw array.',6.4)
d.add_paragraph('The temporal plot sums absolute attribution within the technical and news groups at each input lag, then averages over origins, seeds and references. It describes where the network assigns credit within its input sequence. It is not a real world event response time or a causal impulse response.')
picture(d,'SUBGROUP_AND_PRECISION.png','Left uses input defined groups. Right shows absolute residual divided by its tolerance on a logarithmic scale; values above zero fail the check.',6.4)
d.add_paragraph('Positive and negative XRP news groups require positive or negative stance with nonzero XRP specificity at the forecast origin. High volatility uses the 90th percentile of training origin volatility. Current hour presence means a new article is recorded in that hour; an empty hour can still follow earlier news in the input window. These groups overlap and are descriptive. They are not independently verified regulatory or political announcements and cannot establish an event caused a price reversal. Publication times remain historical availability proxies.')
pageheading(d,'Numerical verification and reproducibility')
table(d,['Seed','Reference','Mean absolute residual','Maximum residual','Points used 64 128 256'],[[int(r.seed),int(r.background),f'{r.mean_abs_residual:.3g}',f'{r.max_abs_residual:.3g}',f'{int(r.q64)} / {int(r.q128)} / {int(r.q256)}'] for _,r in C.iterrows()])
d.add_paragraph('The consolidated review loaded every saved array, checked finite values and 1,000 by 30 by 25 dimensions, verified origin and reference identities against the first explanation run, confirmed references belong to the training origins, and confirmed all five checkpoint hashes match the frozen protocol. Stored completeness residuals were independently recomputed from output differences and attribution sums within floating point tolerance. The 52 failures are 0.52% of all explanations and 5.2% of one pass; their maximum absolute residual is about 0.00278 log return units. The adaptive rule was predeclared and no further integration passes were launched after this review.')
d.add_heading('Saved files',1)
d.add_paragraph('results preserves ten NPZ arrays with all attribution, origin, reference, feature, quadrature and residual dimensions. review preserves individual residuals, pass contributions, feature rankings, temporal and subgroup tables, seed stability and pilot convergence. figures contains all four charts. FULL_PROTOCOL.json records the method and checkpoint hashes. code/pilot.py and code/run.py reproduce the explanation computation. The runner refuses to overwrite an existing run; reproduce costly calculations only in an isolated copy with updated paths. Preserve the run guard and original outputs.')
d.add_heading('Commands for this saved run',1)
